{"name":"Wind Tunnel","hex":"#c7dfe6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wind tunnel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A test facility through which air is forced in a controlled manner so as to study the effects of flow around airfoils, aircraft, motor cars etc.","A space where air currents are naturally funneled through sets of walls or structures, like alleyways or between high-rise buildings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind_tunnel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wind tunnel","blocks":[{"text":"A wind tunnel is \"an apparatus for producing a controlled stream of air for conducting aerodynamic experiments\". The experiment is conducted in the test section of the wind tunnel and a complete tunnel configuration includes air ducting to and from the test section and a device for keeping the air in motion, such as a fan. Wind tunnel uses include assessing the effects of air on an aircraft in flight or a ground vehicle moving on land, and measuring the effect of wind on buildings and bridges. Wind tunnel test sections range in size from less than a foot across, to over 100 feet (30 m), and with air speeds from a light breeze to hypersonic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/8-Foot_Transonic_Pressure_Tunnel_%289443013405%29.jpg/330px-8-Foot_Transonic_Pressure_Tunnel_%289443013405%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind_tunnel","wikidata":"Q193010"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind","wikidata":"Q8094"},{"title":"Tunnel","blocks":[{"text":"A tunnel is an underground or undersea passageway. It is dug through surrounding soil, earth or rock, or laid under water, and is usually completely enclosed except for the two portals common at each end, though there may be access and ventilation openings at various points along the length. A pipeline differs significantly from a tunnel, though some recent tunnels have used immersed tube construction techniques rather than traditional tunnel boring methods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Signalisation_routi%C3%A8re_entr%C3%A9e_sud_tunnel_du_Galibier.jpg/330px-Signalisation_routi%C3%A8re_entr%C3%A9e_sud_tunnel_du_Galibier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunnel","wikidata":"Q44377"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Aeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG/500px-Aeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Aeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG/1280px-Aeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Aeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG/500px-Aeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The effect of streamlining is made visible in a wind tunnel. Shaping the body to make it more streamlined reduces fuel consumption.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAeroakustik-Windkanal-Messhalle.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Wright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg/500px-Wright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Wright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg/1280px-Wright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Wright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg/500px-Wright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Replica of the Wright brothers' wind tunnel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWright_Brothers_Wind_Tunnel_Replica.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Messerschmitt_Bf_109E_wind_tunnel_testing_at_the_Deutsche_LFA.jpg/500px-Messerschmitt_Bf_109E_wind_tunnel_testing_at_the_Deutsche_LFA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Messerschmitt_Bf_109E_wind_tunnel_testing_at_the_Deutsche_LFA.jpg/500px-Messerschmitt_Bf_109E_wind_tunnel_testing_at_the_Deutsche_LFA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Herman Goering tunnel A3 commissioned in 1940[12] showing open test section with Messerschmitt Bf 109F installed for testing.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMesserschmitt_Bf_109E_wind_tunnel_testing_at_the_Deutsche_LFA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg/500px-Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg/1280px-Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg/500px-Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mary Jackson with a wind tunnel model at Langley Research Center","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg/500px-16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg/1280px-16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg/500px-16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fan blades of Langley Research Center's 16-foot transonic wind tunnel in 1990, before it was retired in 2004","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A16_Foot_Transonic_Tunnel_Rehabilitation_-_GPN-2000-001300.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Kirsten_wind_tunnel_08A.jpg/500px-Kirsten_wind_tunnel_08A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Kirsten_wind_tunnel_08A.jpg/1280px-Kirsten_wind_tunnel_08A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thum